# Concept DOI of the archived releases; it always resolves to the latest version.
# The version tag and the release date of each archived release are those of the
# corresponding Zenodo version.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21731939
repository-code: https://github.com/shb115/shadow-cpa
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Target firmware, acquisition scripts and analysis code for a non-profiling
  correlation power analysis of the Shadow lightweight block cipher. All traces
  were acquired on a ChipWhisperer-Nano capture board with its on-board
  STM32F030F4 target, clocked at 7.5 MHz with one sample per clock cycle and
  firmware built at optimization level -O0. The code covers Shadow-32 with a
  fixed key, Shadow-32 with ten independently chosen keys, and Shadow-64, the
  fixed-key attack at two further clock phases, the characterization of the
  leakage model on the device, and the attack and the fixed-versus-random
  t-tests, at first and second order, of two masked Shadow-32 implementations
  (an ISW gadget and table recomputation with register overwriting), each over
  one whole masked round in two independent acquisitions and over the full
  16-round encryption. The power traces it analyzes are archived separately;
  see the related identifier below.
keywords:
  - side-channel analysis
  - correlation power analysis
  - lightweight block cipher
  - Shadow
  - masking
  - leakage assessment
references:
  - type: data
    title: >-
      Power traces for "Practical Key Recovery on the Shadow Lightweight Block
      Cipher with Non-Profiling Correlation Power Analysis"
